Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(brand):=20rename=20Allocate=20=E2=86=92=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?Cairn=20across=20metadata,=20UI,=20and=20brand=20assets?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The product name "Allocate" was too descriptive of a single feature
(monthly allocation). Cairn — a stack of stones that marks a trail —
captures the whole product better: every saving, fund, and monthly plan
is a stone on the user's financial journey.

This is a **rename-only** change. The `allocate` verb (and derived
identifiers like `unallocatedFunds`, `overAllocated`, `AllocationSummary`,
`sectionUnallocated`) still describes the underlying action and is left
as-is throughout the codebase and i18n strings.

Metadata & package:
- package.json / package-lock.json: `name` → `cairn`
- app/layout.tsx: title, appleWebApp.title, description
- app/manifest.ts: name, short_name, description, theme_color, background_color
- .braingrid/project.json: project_name (repo identity fields untouched)
- README.md: heading + lead paragraph now use the cairn metaphor

UI copy & branding:
- Landing page (app/page.tsx): header and footer brand mark replaced —
  the purple "A" gradient tile is swapped for the donut icon (served from
  /cairn-icon.svg). The larger landing-page palette (violet gradients,
  CTA buttons) is intentionally left for a follow-up design pass.
- Nav components (Header, Sidebar, MobileDrawer): "Allocate" → "Cairn",
  collapsed sidebar monogram "A" → "C"
- Screenshot generator: text labels updated for the Android PWA install
  preview

Theme colors:
- viewport.themeColor and manifest.theme_color: `#7c3aed` (violet) →
  navy palette matching the donut icon (#0F2A4A dark, #f8fafc light)
- manifest.background_color: now #0F2A4A so the PWA splash is cohesive
  with the icon

Brand assets:
- Renamed public/allocate-icon.svg → public/cairn-icon.svg
- Renamed public/allocate-icon-transparent.svg → public/cairn-icon-transparent.svg
- Added public/cairn-wordmark.svg (light) and public/cairn-wordmark-dark.svg
- scripts/generate-icons.mjs emits the new filenames

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
